    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "I added a Dashboard page that shows how many clients and projects you have and how much you're still owed. `bin/e2e` passes: with the seeded data the page shows 2 clients, 2 projects and an outstanding total of `300.00`, which is the two unpaid invoices (100 + 200) and leaves out the paid one.\n\nTwo things differ from the request:\n- **No database migration.** The page only reads totals from the tables you already have, so nothing in the schema needed to change.\n- **The server is Spring Boot, not OfficeFloor.** The request said OfficeFloor, but the app (and `CLAUDE.md`) uses Spring Boot, so I followed that.\n\n**Server (`dashboard` package)**\n- `InvoiceRepository.sumAmountByStatus(status)` is a new query that adds up invoice amounts for one status and returns 0 when there are none.\n- `DashboardService` uses the existing repository counts plus the unpaid sum, rounded to 2 decimal places.\n- `DashboardController` serves this as `GET /api/dashboard`, returning `{ clients, projects, outstanding }`.\n\n**Front end**\n- `features/dashboard/dashboard.service.ts` fetches those figures.\n- `features/dashboard/dashboard.ts` shows them, formats the total with 2 decimal places, and shows a loading message or an error message when needed.\n- One new route, `dashboard`, in `app.routes.ts`. The nav bar picks it up automatically as `nav-dashboard`, and it appears first, just before Home.\n- The test ids match the spec: `dashboard-clients-count`, `dashboard-projects-count` and `dashboard-outstanding-total`.\n\nDecision for you: opening the app (`/`) still goes to the existing empty Home page, so the dashboard is a separate nav link. I didn't change this because other tests may expect that page at `/`. If you want the dashboard to be the home screen, pointing `/` at it is a one-line change to the redirect in `app.routes.ts`.",
